**ARTICLE IX: INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY**

9.1 **Ownership of Intellectual Property**

(a) All intellectual property developed, invented, or conceived during the course of this Agreement related to Innovex-123, including but not limited to formulations, methodologies, protocols, data, and results arising from the Clinical Trials, shall be jointly owned by GCR and PII. Each party shall have the right to use such jointly owned intellectual property for their respective purposes, subject to the terms of this Agreement.

(b) In the event that either party wishes to file for patent protection on any jointly owned intellectual property, they must provide written notice to the other party at least thirty (30) days prior to filing. Both parties shall collaborate in good faith to determine the scope of the patent application and share the costs associated with the patent filing process equally.

9.2 **Confidentiality of Intellectual Property**

(a) Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of any proprietary information related to Innovex-123 and its development, including trade secrets and intellectual property, that is disclosed during the term of this Agreement. This confidentiality obligation shall survive the termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years.

(b) GCR and PII shall implement reasonable safeguards to protect the confidentiality of such information, including limiting access to personnel who require it for the performance of their duties under this Agreement.

**ARTICLE X: ADDITIONAL COLLABORATIVE EFFORTS**

10.1 **Joint Steering Committee**

(a) The parties agree to establish a Joint Steering Committee (JSC) comprised of an equal number of representatives from both PII and GCR to oversee the collaboration, review progress, and address any operational issues arising during the execution of this Agreement.

(b) The JSC shall meet quarterly, or more frequently if necessary, to discuss the status of the Clinical Trials, review data, and evaluate the overall progress of Innovex-123's development. Minutes of each meeting shall be documented and shared with both parties.

10.2 **Collaborative Research Initiatives**

(a) In addition to the Clinical Trials, both parties may agree to undertake collaborative research initiatives aimed at further exploring the potential of Innovex-123. This may include additional studies, post-marketing research, or exploring additional indications.

(b) Funding for such initiatives will be subject to mutual agreement and shall be documented in separate agreements detailing the scope of work, responsibilities, and financial arrangements.

**ARTICLE XI: REGULATORY COMPLIANCE**

11.1 **Regulatory Responsibilities**

(a) PII shall be responsible for obtaining and maintaining all necessary regulatory approvals and licenses required for the development, testing, and commercialization of Innovex-123, including but not limited to Investigational New Drug (IND) applications and New Drug Applications (NDA) with the Food and Drug Administration (FDA).

(b) GCR shall provide PII with all necessary data and information generated from the Clinical Trials to support the regulatory submissions, adhering to all applicable regulations and guidelines.

11.2 **Quality Assurance and Compliance**

(a) Both parties agree to comply with all relevant Good Clinical Practice (GCP) guidelines and applicable regulatory requirements during the conduct of the Clinical Trials and any associated activities.

(b) GCR shall conduct regular audits of clinical trial sites and processes to ensure compliance, and shall promptly report any non-compliance issues to PII.

**ARTICLE XII: INDEMNIFICATION AND LIABILITY**

12.1 **Indemnification**

(a) Each party shall indemnify and hold harmless the other party, its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorney’s fees) arising from the negligent or willful misconduct of the indemnifying party in connection with this Agreement.

(b) This indemnification obligation shall survive the termination of this Agreement.

12.2 **Limitation of Liability**

(a) Except for liability arising from breaches of confidentiality or indemnification obligations, neither party shall be liable to the other for any indirect, special, incidental, or consequential damages arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, even if such party has been advised of the possibility of such damages.

(b) The aggregate liability of either party for any claim arising out of this Agreement shall not exceed the total amount paid by PII to GCR under this Agreement.

